@startuml clock-budget
!include common.iuml
title clock budget controller, one move

start
:side to move, bank = remaining, moves played = n;
:budget draw (idempotent per move);
:spendable = max(0, remaining - SearchSafetyMarginMs);
:movesLeft = max(1, ClockExpectedMovesPerSide - n);
:feedforward = spendable / movesLeft + increment x ClockIncrementShare;
:error = remaining - target,\ntarget = drain trajectory\nfloored at SearchSafetyMarginMs;
:correction = clamp(pid(error),\n+ or - ClockPIDClampFraction x feedforward);
:grant = clamp(feedforward + correction,\nSearchMinMoveTimeMs,\nmax(spendable, SearchMinMoveTimeMs));
note right
  the floor wins over the reserve:
  a fully drained 1+0 clock still
  funds SearchMinMoveTimeMs moves,
  remaining never goes negative, a
  timeout can never decide a game
end note
:search runs on the grant;
:commit: remaining = max(0, remaining - elapsed) + increment,\nn = n + 1;
if (game continues?) then (yes)
  :next move draws a fresh budget;
  stop
else (no)
  stop
endif
@enduml
